id: pm-rust-2tb9
title: Validate mutation identifiers before acquiring locks
description: A synthetic scratch tracker and directory event watcher confirm that claiming an unknown path-bearing identifier creates and removes a transient lock outside the locks directory before item discovery refuses it. Lock acquisition in src/mutation.rs joins the caller identifier before validation. This predates the selection lifecycle slice and applies to the shared mutation boundary.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: mutation,safety,validation
created_at: "2026-10-13T13:19:32.970Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T13:23:56.928Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Reject path separators, absolute identifiers and traversal forms before lock creation; real scratch trackers prove that malformed IDs cause no filesystem writes and valid canonical ownership and mutation IDs retain published parity."
parent: pm-rust-u4al
